  "every-summer-after": {
    "id": "every-summer-after",
    "title": "Every Summer After",
    "category": "fiction",
    "body": "<p class=\"mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-[#CCCCCC]\">Lagi-lagi, rekomendasi novel bahasa Inggris terpopuler selanjutnya terpilih juga sebagai nominasi buku fiksi dan buku debut terbaik pada tahun 2022. Nah, novelnya berjudul Every Summer After yang ditulis oleh Carley Fortune.</p><p class=\"mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-[#CCCCCC]\">Pernahkah kamu merasa bahwa kesalahan yang pernah dilakukan bisa membatasi masa depanmu? Kalau pernah, mungkin sinopsis dari novel ini cukup relate untukmu.</p><p class=\"mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-[#CCCCCC]\">Novel Every Summer After menceritakan tokoh bernama Persephone Fraser yang selalu dihantui rasa khawatir akan masa depan sejak ia melakukan kesalahan besar pada 10 tahun lalu.</p><p class=\"mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-[#CCCCCC]\">Saat musim panas, ia menjalani hari-hari di sebuah apartemen modern tengah kota dan kerap menghabiskan waktu bersama teman-temannya.</p><p class=\"mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-[#CCCCCC]\">Sampai akhirnya, hidup Persephone berubah ketika ia menerima telepon yang mengirimnya kembali ke Barry\u2019s Bay, dan juga kembali ke kehidupan Sam Florek.</p>"
  },
  "ferry-harbourfront": {
    "id": "ferry-harbourfront",
    "title": "The 3:00 AM Ferry to HarbourFront",
    "subtitle": "Reflections on the dark water between two countries, carrying a laptop and big ambitions.",
    "category": "slice-of-life",
    "badgeText": "Slice of Life \u2022 Journey",
    "badgeClass": "bg-slate-500/20 text-slate-300 border-slate-500/30",
    "color": "slate",
    "readTime": "5 min read",
    "date": "June 2026",
    "location": "Singapore Strait Crossing",
    "quote": "Crossing an international border by sea reminds you how arbitrary distances really are.",
    "image": "images/stories/ferry-harbourfront.jpg",
    "tags": [
      "#FerryCrossing",
      "#Ambition",
      "#SeaBreeze"
    ],
    "excerpt": "Gliding across the dark Singapore Strait aboard a passenger ferry. Looking out the salt-streaked window at cargo ship beacons while clutching a backpack full of dreams and code.",
    "initialCoffees": 46,
    "body": "\n            <p class=\"first-letter:float-left first-letter:text-6xl first-letter:font-extrabold first-letter:text-slate-300 first-letter:mr-3 first-letter:leading-none\">\n                The twin diesel engines of the catamaran vibrated through the steel hull with a deep, hypnotic rhythm.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n                Outside the salt-filmed window, the water was inky black. We were slicing across the international shipping channel of the Singapore Strait\u2014one of the busiest maritime arteries on the planet. Hundreds of colossal container ships and crude oil tankers were anchored across the water, their deck cranes and red navigational beacons glowing like floating cities.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n                Inside the cabin, the air conditioning was ice-cold. Most passengers were asleep, heads propped against vinyl headrests.\n            </p>\n            <h4 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2\"><i class=\"fas fa-ship text-slate-300\"></i> Between Two Worlds</h4>\n            <p>\n                I clutched my canvas backpack against my chest. Inside was my trusty laptop, a worn notebook, my passport, and a presentation deck for a software engineering conference in Singapore.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n                Growing up in the Riau Islands, you live in the constant shadow of a global metropolis. You can see the high-rises of the financial district on clear afternoons, yet between here and there lies a border, a passport stamp, and forty minutes of open sea.\n            </p>\n            <blockquote class=\"border-l-4 border-slate-400 pl-4 py-2 my-6 text-slate-200 italic bg-slate-900/40 rounded-r-xl\">\n                \"The ocean doesn't care about passports. It only asks whether your vessel is sturdy enough to handle the swells.\"\n            </blockquote>\n            <p>\n                I opened my laptop lid and reviewed the architecture slide. The microservices were solid. The API contracts were cleanly decoupled. The test coverage was at 94%.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n                As the ferry rounded the southern tip of Sentosa, the glittering towers of HarbourFront and Marina Bay rose from the sea like a mountain of glass and light. I took a deep breath, zipped up my jacket, and smiled. The boat was docking. It was time to show the world what we could build.\n            </p>\n        "
  },
